INT. OPEN-PLAN OFFICE - "SYNERGY HUB" - MORNING

Standing desks, bean bags, a kombucha tap, motivational posters. A banner: "WE ARE FAMILY." A beanbag chair shaped like a unicorn. Fluorescent morning light.

TARQUIN "TARK" BOLLINGER, 30s, in a vest and sneakers, balances on a wobble board. Beside him, CORDELIA "CORDY" ADESANYA, 40s, hair in a tight bun, taps at a laptop. MARGUERITE LESAGE-OKORO, 50s, the office manager, hoses a droopy fern. THADDEUS "THAD" QUILLFEATHER, 60s, a quiet man in a gray suit, sits at the corner desk, unmoving.

TARK
Team! Quick sync!

CORDY
We just did a sync.

TARK
This is a meta-sync.

MARGUERITE
(over the hose)
Tark, the fern is dying.

TARK
Everything is dying. That's the culture of change.

Cordy rolls her eyes. Thad stays still. He has not moved in some time.

TARK (CONT'D)
Thad. Buddy. Thoughts?

No answer.

CORDY
Thad?

MARGUERITE
Thad doesn't talk before ten.

TARK
It's ten-fifteen.

CORDY
Is he, uh...

MARGUERITE
He's fine.

TARK
He's on mute.

CORDY
We're in person.

TARK
Mute is a state of mind.

They approach the desk. Marguerite prods Thad's shoulder with the hose. He topples out of the chair. Cordy shrieks. Tark falls off the wobble board. Marguerite drops the hose, which sprays everyone. They scramble backward. Thad lies on the floor, eyes closed, and snores.

CORDY
He's asleep!

MARGUERITE
He's been asleep since Tuesday.

TARK
Since Tuesday?

MARGUERITE
That's when he stopped answering emails.

TARK
We thought that was mindfulness.

Thad opens one eye. Sits up, slowly, dripping.

THAD
Is it Friday?

CORDY
It's Thursday.

THAD
Damn.

He lies back down. Tark stares at the others. Cordy stares at Marguerite. Marguerite shuts off the water.

TARK
Okay. New initiative. Naps.

CORDY
We already have naps.

TARK
Mandatory naps.

THAD
(from the floor, dreamy)
I'd back that.

MARGUERITE
Tark, who signed off on the quarterly?

TARK
Which quarterly?

MARGUERITE
The one that says we're out of money.

TARK
We're out of money?

CORDY
We've been out of money since March.

TARK
But the kombucha tap works.

MARGUERITE
That's a donation.

Tark takes a long, wobbly step. He looks at the banner. At the unicorn beanbag. At the dying fern. Behind him, the overhead lights flicker out one by one.

THAD
(softly)
Told you.

TARK
Told me what?

THAD
That it was Friday.
